WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.305
- [Interviewer] All right, Kristen.

00:00:02.305 --> 00:00:03.138
- Yes, sir.

00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:03.971
- [Interviewer] Kristen,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:04.804
Where are you from originally?

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.890
- I was born in Fort Worth, Texas.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.170
I came out here when my mom

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.860
decided to find my dad,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.570
and I came out here when
I was about two years old.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.920
Mom got into a heroin
addiction and never left.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.920
- [Interviewer] So you came
down to Skid Row at what age?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.800
- I was two when I came down here.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.070
- [Interviewer] Two?

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.037
- I grew up down here,
sad to say. (chuckling)

00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:28.870
But this is home.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.860
- [Interviewer] And
how was your childhood?

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.613
- Dysfunctional, very, very dysfunctional.

00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:35.521
- [Interviewer] I'll bet.

00:00:35.521 --> 00:00:38.543
- My dad was a drug dealer
and my mom was a prostitute.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.630
I got sold into prostitution by my mom

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:44.973
to support her habit.

00:00:45.896 --> 00:00:46.729
- [Interviewer] At what age?

00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:48.593
- I was 11 when my mom sold me.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.240
August 3rd of 1996.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.810
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.300
What is that like for a young
girl to start doing that?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.163
- Scary.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.483
It's depressing.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.283
And it's, once you get into that life,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.653
I was in it 20 years before
I was finally able to

00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:17.180
make my break, and some
girls never make a break.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.180
So I mean, this life will
scar you in ways that

00:01:22.597 --> 00:01:23.823
you never see coming.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.633
- [Interviewer] So how was your
relationship with your mom?

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.733
- My mom's and I relationship,

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.410
even though she did what she did,

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.510
she was still my best friend.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.860
We talked about everything,
did everything together.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.010
- [Interviewer] Is she still around?

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.673
- My mom committed suicide 20 years ago.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.770
- [Interviewer] And how old were you then?

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.420
- I was 14.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.520
- [Interviewer] Oh my god.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.120
So at 14, you're on your own down here?

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.000
Or was dad, did dad come into the picture?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.223
- No, my dad was in and out
the picture long before that.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.880
My dad did 17 years in the penitentiary

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.180
for strong-armed robbery
and attempted murder.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.470
So, I never really got to meet my dad

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.580
up until a couple of years ago.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.430
But from the time my mom died,
I was pretty much on my own.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.050
I mean, my grandpa was there.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.240
He's my hero.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.190
He took on me and my
eight brothers and sisters

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.296
after mom died.
- Oh, so you went to

00:02:23.296 --> 00:02:24.129
your grandparents after your mom died?

00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:25.630
- I went to my grandpa.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.160
I never knew my grandma, she
died giving birth to my mom.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.472
- [Interviewer] Oh, I see.

00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:30.777
- I never got to know her,

00:02:30.777 --> 00:02:33.300
but my grandpa was my hero for that.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.580
He took on a lot of kids.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.493
Badass kids, too.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.650
We were a rough bunch. (chuckling)

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.230
- [Interviewer] So today,
you're living in a tent?

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.200
- I live in a tent a block
and a half from here.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.863
- [Interviewer] And what
are you doing for money now?

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.530
- Anything that I can without getting

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.730
into no legal troubles.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.530
- [Interviewer] What have you
done for money over the years?

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.150
- I've been a prostitute, I've
been a part-time drug dealer.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.283
I've been an enforcer for
some of the dealers down here.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.190
All the things that people don't wanna do,

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.570
I've done. (chuckling)

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.320
- [Interviewer] And
what is your drug today?

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.124
- [Kristen] I'm a crystal meth addict.

00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:14.240
- [Interviewer] Crystal meth.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.610
What does crystal meth do
for you, at this point?

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.419
'Cause you've been doing it for how long?

00:03:18.419 --> 00:03:20.801
- [Kristen] I've been
doing it since I was 13.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:21.634
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.940
- [Kristen] It's just a habit.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.230
It's just like another
person smoking a cigarette.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.423
It's just, it's a comfort.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.960
It's a social drug, I don't
like to smoke by myself.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.890
And otherwise, I'm a
pretty introverted person.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.036
I don't hang out with everybody,

00:03:39.036 --> 00:03:42.530
I don't mess with everybody,
so it's my way to be social

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.010
and not be a complete wallflower.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.932
- [Interviewer] It makes
you more extroverted?

00:03:46.932 --> 00:03:47.765
- [Kristen] Huh?

00:03:47.765 --> 00:03:48.598
- [Interviewer] It makes
you more extroverted?

00:03:48.598 --> 00:03:50.523
- [Kristen] Yeah, extroverted, definitely.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.910
- [Interviewer] And then,

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.480
you've been down here
for decades and decades.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.340
I'm sure you've seen some crazy things.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.200
- [Kristen] I've seen people
burned alive in Porta Potties

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.660
for $5 worth of crack.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:07.490
I've seen bodies fly out of
windows 12 and 13 stories up.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.630
I've seen countless suicides.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.470
- [Interviewer] Was
that the Frontier Hotel?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.237
- [Kristen] Yep, Frontier.

00:04:12.237 --> 00:04:14.580
The Frontier, the Alexandria, the Rosin,

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.343
they all used to be bad, real bad.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.383
Yep.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.540
I've seen people get killed.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.563
I've seen people stabbed, beat.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.520
Just last year, one of my
best friends was beat to death

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.870
and stabbed to death,
down here on Sam's Union.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.510
- [Interviewer] What was the
lowest point in your life?

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.093
- I would say the lowest point in my life,

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.280
the day my youngest daughter was born.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.473
She was born with human
feces in her lungs,

00:04:48.536 --> 00:04:51.373
and it was behind my
crystal meth addiction.

00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:55.640
I was too caught up in
getting high and being popular

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.853
to put the pipe down.

00:04:59.915 --> 00:05:01.230
- [Interviewer] So you didn't raise her?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.063
You lost her?

00:05:02.063 --> 00:05:04.340
- She never came home from the hospital.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.690
She went straight into an adopted family.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.150
- [Interviewer] How many kids do you have?

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.263
- I have six kids and two grandkids.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.650
- [Interviewer] Did you raise your kids?

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.483
Any of them?

00:05:17.621 --> 00:05:20.920
- The last one to be born,
I didn't have any hand

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.210
in her raising, but the other five,

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.263
I had them for a partial
time in their life, I did.

00:05:30.626 --> 00:05:33.290
- [Interviewer] Do you
ever talk to your kids now?

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.457
- I haven't talked to my kids since 2013.

00:05:36.457 --> 00:05:37.533
- [Interviewer] Oh, wow.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.570
Do you see a connection between

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.720
the childhood that you had that was--

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.870
- It's a repetitive cycle.
- Certainly difficult, right?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.330
And in your life today?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.463
- It is, it's a very repetitive cycle.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.463
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
the role models you had,

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.727
the environment--
- The drug dealers and pimps

00:05:55.727 --> 00:05:58.920
and the hoes, and it's still,

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.010
even not being in that
life, I can't shake it.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:05.521
I can't shake the
consequences of being in it.

00:06:05.521 --> 00:06:06.977
- [Interviewer] If there
was anything about your life

00:06:06.977 --> 00:06:10.363
you could've changed, what would that be?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.170
- That's a good question.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.650
With having so many things I would change,

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.300
I can't find just one.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.450
But I think the biggest one I would change

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.973
is never picking up a pipe.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.870
- [Interviewer] And then
also, last time you mentioned

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.780
having a dad in your life.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.100
- Yeah.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.563
I would definitely have my dad in my life.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:46.360
And it's hard for a girl not having a dad,

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.540
because all of the education
and all the lessons

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.230
that we're supposed to learn,

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:55.583
about how to pick a good
guy later on in life.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.920
Most girls learn that
lesson from their dad,

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:02.363
watching their dad, and
I can't say that I did.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.760
I believe that if I would've
had my dad in my life as a kid,

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.060
it would've been a little
bit different today.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.100
- [Interviewer] What kind
of guys do you end up

00:07:12.539 --> 00:07:13.539
hooking up with now?

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.003
- Drug dealers, abusers.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.550
Guys that don't really
want nothing in life

00:07:22.483 --> 00:07:24.363
but to be ghetto famous.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.420
- [Interviewer] Do you have
any hope of getting clean

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.770
and getting off the street?

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:37.050
- Logically, part of me
wants to say yeah, I do.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:40.113
But in reality, at this
point in life, probably not.

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:42.990
- [Interviewer] Do you
think you'll be down here

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.213
for the rest of your life?

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.153
- Yeah.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:55.683
Being down here so long, it becomes home.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.140
And nobody really wants to leave home.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.413
- [Interviewer] All right, Kristen.

00:08:05.413 --> 00:08:06.246
Thank you so much for talking to me.

00:08:06.246 --> 00:08:07.093
- Thank you.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.370
- [Interviewer] Good luck with everything.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.203
- Thank you.

00:08:15.049 --> 00:08:16.632
I'm such a crybaby.

00:08:18.143 --> 00:08:18.976
- [Interviewer] No,
you've been through hell.

00:08:18.976 --> 00:08:20.120
And you probably don't
get to talk about this

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.937
very often, right?
- Nope.

